WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.675
Here's the idea the rest
of the talk builds on.

2
00:00:02.675 --> 00:00:08.399
Almost every name in this path is public
and owned by a vendor: Oracle's Fusion

3
00:00:08.399 --> 00:00:10.853
host, Microsoft Graph and sign-in,

4
00:00:10.853 --> 00:00:14.487
the agent's relay names,
the Amazon Connect names.

5
00:00:14.487 --> 00:00:19.316
The agency's job is to resolve those
correctly from every resolver a component

6
00:00:19.316 --> 00:00:23.476
can reach, and never to host or shadow
them in a private zone of its own.

7
00:00:23.476 --> 00:00:29.241
Private DNS and forwarding are needed in
only four places: names the agency owns,

8
00:00:29.241 --> 00:00:34.746
like AD domains, cloud private endpoints
the middleware uses, cloud private

9
00:00:34.746 --> 00:00:40.687
zones on-premises systems must read, and
AWS interface endpoints with private DNS.

10
00:00:40.687 --> 00:00:43.726
Everything else is ordinary
public resolution.

11
00:00:43.726 --> 00:00:45.770
So where does each component look?
